/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (Front Wing The front wing is the first point of contact with airflow, crucial for minimising drag and frontal area and optimising aerodynamics. A key function is reducing wheel wake, where rotating wheels create turbulence that disrupts downstream airflow. By directing air over the wheels, the front wing ensures cleaner airflow and improved efficiency. It also mitigates the Magnus effect, which causes uneven pressure distribution on spinning wheels, increasing drag and lift. )
/E (Front Wing The front wing is the first point of contact with airflow, crucial for minimising drag and frontal area and optimising aerodynamics. A key function is reducing wheel wake, where rotating wheels create turbulence that disrupts downstream airflow. By directing air over the wheels, the front wing ensures cleaner airflow and improved efficiency. It also mitigates the Magnus effect, which causes uneven pressure distribution on spinning wheels, increasing drag and lift. )
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [15 16]
>>
