/S /P
/E (The support structures are created to ensure structural integrity and avoid any breaks that may occur. The ramps on the side are responsible for shovelling airflow over the wheels and channelling the air in a way to maximise laminar flow, reducing the drag force and providing stability. We went for a minimal design to minimise drag, frontal area and weight. The support structures are positioned strategically to hide them behind the wingspan to minimise obstruction to airflow.)
/Pg 10 0 R
