/E (The regional wheels had internal spokes, which required hub caps to ensure smooth airflow and protect internal geometry, but this increased the overall weight and Moment of Inertia\(MOI=197 at 14mm thickness\). In response, the wheels were redesigned without spokes to reduce mass. Three prototypes with varied dimensions were tested, and the design was adjusted to meet the updated regulation mandating a minimum rear wheel thickness of 17 mm and a front of 13 mm.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [19 20]
>>
