/E (Nimbus is Latin for a thundercloud. Built to minimise area and increase straight-line speed, Nimbus was where we tested out two of our innovations: tilted sidepods and the vortex teeth. The front wing was kept consistent, as we believed its design was fairly optimised. We also made a change to the rear wing: by sweeping it around the body, we were able to cut down the area it was taking up. The diffusers were also modelled in an aerofoil shape to reduce the wake. It was significantly slimmer than the earlier prototype Tonitrum, but was ultimately deemed non-manufacturable.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [35]
>>
