/E (performance but also on feasibility, stock fit, and cutter behaviour. The adoption of CAM helped us bridge the gap between design and execution, enabling a more reliable, efficient, and production ready workflow.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [48]
>>
endobj
562 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (During the regional stage, CAM and CNC analysis software were not utilised in the development process. As a result, several design aspects failed to meet manufacturing regulations, leading to significant mark deductions. The absence of toolpath simulation, stock dimension validation, and material removal analysis resulted in parts that were not manufacturing-ready. Recognising this gap, we made a major shift in our workflow for the national round by integrating CAM software into our design pipeline. This allowed us to simulate tool paths, test machining strategies, and ensure that every design was dimensionally accurate and compatible with CNC machining standards from the start.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
